{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>You shall not make abominable, etc.</b> One needs to know why He returned yet again to give this commandment? And our Sages of blessed memory (in Torat Kohanim) said: to include that which detached and returned. Now this exposition is true, but it seems unnecessary — once they have detached, is it because they returned that they would be permitted? And one must settle their words of blessed memory. Perhaps the verse comes to inform us that one who eats of the creeping creatures will make his very soul into a creeping creature, and this is the meaning of <b>you shall not make abominable your souls</b> — meaning, do not make your souls an abomination — and with what? <b>with any creeping creature that creeps upon the earth</b>, when you eat of it. And go now and see what we wrote in parashat Bereshit at the hint of the verse (Genesis 1:26) ״וְיִרְדּוּ בִדְגַת הַיָּם״, etc. And you will find the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Pesachim 49b) concerning the unlearned masses: they are a creeping creature, and their daughters are an abomination, etc. And all their words of blessed memory were spoken in the holy spirit, and they are our very own words." "And the verse's saying <b>and you shall not defile yourselves through them</b> — perhaps it intends to say that Israel must be careful lest they enter their mouths even involuntarily (בְּהֶסֵחַ הַדַּעַת), for the distinction between inadvertent and intentional in this matter is such that inadvertent is like intentional, since the revulsion does its work in a person's soul even involuntarily; only that the blemish differs — in an intentional act one's soul becomes an abomination, and in an inadvertent act one's soul becomes defiled and impure. And this is the meaning of <b>and you shall not defile yourselves and you shall become impure through them.</b> And a person must exercise added caution and vigilance in anything that falls under the category of doubt regarding this abomination, and all the more so in these times when the air and all the lands together have become polluted, and there is no produce of the land that does not contain some of the abomination — whoever guards his soul will guard this matter."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:32.725298691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}